  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for textbook topic 4.6 (page 119): a nuclear power plant on a river bank at dusk, cut open: the control rods rise, the core glows blue in its water, steam runs to the turbine, the turbine and generator turn, power runs along the lines and a town's windows light up. The student picks the fuel's mass (1 g to 1 kg of uranium-235) and whether it is split (0.079% of its mass becomes energy) or turned fully into energy as E = mc² says; the panel gives E in J (c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s, as the book) and how long it would light a 100 W bulb. Sizes are not to scale (said in the panel). Three test questions (E = mc² for a few grams, which part makes the electricity, why so much energy). Offline, Bangla and English.",
